	(text "Interlock (hardware, independent of firmware):\n  TMC_DRV_ENN = NAND(DRV_EN, E_OK)      -> driver off unless Pico enables it AND E-stop loop closed\n  CLUTCH_*    = AND(Pico request, E_OK) -> clutch off on E-stop\nPico outputs have pull-downs so everything is off while the Pico is in reset.\nE-stop: NC contact between ESTOP_SRC (+3V3 via 330R) and ESTOP_RET. Open or broken wire -> E_OK low.\nThe Pico only reads E_OK through 100k (E_OK_SENSE), so firmware can never hold the interlock enabled.\nThe E-stop removes driver enable and clutch drive; it does not disconnect the 36 V bus.\nSWD: solder a 3-pin header to the Pico's own SWCLK/GND/SWDIO pads (module edge)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a76ffabf-a803-5084-b234-96f92fb2d140")
	)
